{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:03:20.234Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_353079","parameters":{"description":"Exhaustively search for minimal-size prudent formulas with and without constants","command":"python3 -c '\nimport check\n\n# Count symbols where B, ~ are unary (cost 1), &, |, -> are binary (cost 1), and a, c, d, T, F are leaves (cost 1).\n# Wait: since every formula inside/outside has finite truth tables on relevant histories, let us enumerate by size!\n\ndef gen_formulas(max_size, allow_consts=True):\n    # by_size[s][modalized] = list of string representations\n    leaves_mod = [\"T\", \"F\"] if allow_consts else []\n    leaves_all = ([\"a\", \"c\", \"d\", \"T\", \"F\"] if allow_consts else [\"a\", \"c\", \"d\"])\n    \n    # Wait: to avoid redundant formulas, let us evaluate each formula on a set of test Kripke models (say all histories of length <= 4 over {0..7}^4)\n    # No, for size <= 8 there are very few formulas if we deduplicate by truth table on worlds 0,1,2,3!\n    pass\n\n# Let us count how many syntactic trees exist of size <= 8\n# Size 1: leaves (5 or 3)\n# Unary: ~, B\n# Binary: &, |, ->\ndef search(max_size, allow_consts):\n    atoms = [\"a\", \"c\", \"d\"] + ([\"T\", \"F\"] if allow_consts else [])\n    by_size = {1: [(x, x in (\"T\", \"F\")) for x in atoms]}\n    for s in range(2, max_size + 1):\n        cur = []\n        # Unary\n        for f, mod in by_size.get(s - 1, []):\n            cur.append((f\"~({f})\", mod))\n            cur.append((f\"B({f})\", True))\n        # Binary\n        for s1 in range(1, s - 1):\n            s2 = s - 1 - s1\n            for f1, mod1 in by_size.get(s1, []):\n                for f2, mod2 in by_size.get(s2, []):\n                    m = mod1 and mod2\n                    if s == max_size and not m:\n                        continue\n                    cur.append((f\"({f1})&({f2})\", m))\n                    cur.append((f\"({f1})|({f2})\", m))\n                    cur.append((f\"({f1})->({f2})\", m))\n        by_size[s] = cur\n    return by_size\n\nfor allow_consts in [True, False]:\n    by_size = search(7 if allow_consts else 8, allow_consts)\n    for s in sorted(by_size):\n        mod_fs = [f for f, m in by_size[s] if m]\n        prudent_fs = []\n        for f in mod_fs:\n            d, r = check.outcomes(f)\n            if r[\"CB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"DB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"FB\"] == \"C\" and r[\"FB_reply\"] == \"C\" and r[\"X\"] == \"C\":\n                prudent_fs.append(f)\n        print(f\"allow_consts={allow_consts}, size={s}: total_mod={len(mod_fs)}, prudent={len(prudent_fs)}\")\n        if prudent_fs:\n            for pf in prudent_fs[:10]:\n                print(\"  example:\", pf)\n'"}}
