{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:08:57.049Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_315654","parameters":{"command":"python3 -c '\nimport check\n\n# Let us deduplicate formulas by their evaluation on a small set of histories, or even simpler:\n# Any depth <= 2 formula has its meaning inside depth 1 determined by (v, S) where v in {0..7}, S in P({0..7})!\n# Wait: for our 4 opponents, even more simply, we can deduplicate by truth table on all possible (v, S) pairs!\n# How many (v, S) pairs exist? 8 * 256 = 2048 pairs!\n# A boolean function on 2048 pairs is a 2048-bit integer!\n# Wait: inside B(...), at depth 0, a formula only depends on v in {0..7} (an 8-bit integer)!\n# At depth 1, a formula depends on (v, S) (a 2048-bit integer), and B(depth-0) at (v, S) is True iff S is a subset of the truth set of the depth-0 formula!\n# At depth 2 (fully modalized), does a formula even need all (v, S)?\n# Let us check how many distinct depth-0, depth-1, and depth-2 formulas exist by size!\n\nALL_8 = (1 << 8) - 1\n# Precompute for each 8-bit truth table p (0..255), the 2048-bit truth table of B(p) on (v, S):\n# Pair index: idx = (S << 3) | v, where S in 0..255, v in 0..7.\nB_d0 = [0] * 256\nfor p in range(256):\n    # B(p) holds at (v, S) iff (S & ~p) == 0\n    val = 0\n    not_p = (~p) & 0xFF\n    for S in range(256):\n        if (S & not_p) == 0:\n            val |= (0xFF << (S << 3))\n    B_d0[p] = val\n\nALL_2048 = (1 << 2048) - 1\nv_mask = [0] * 3 # a, c, d masks on 2048 bits\nfor S in range(256):\n    for v in range(8):\n        idx = (S << 3) | v\n        if v & 4: v_mask[0] |= (1 << idx)\n        if v & 2: v_mask[1] |= (1 << idx)\n        if v & 1: v_mask[2] |= (1 << idx)\n\nprint(\"Precomputed masks successfully!\")\n'","description":"Test fast bitmask representation of depth-0 and depth-1 formulas"}}
{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:08:57.715Z","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_315654","status":"success","output":"Precomputed masks successfully!"}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:09:21.496Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_303668","parameters":{"command":"python3 -c '\nimport check\n\n# Let us see how depth <= 1 formulas (which are 2048-bit ints) and depth <= 2 fully modalized formulas behave.\n# Wait: what is the semantic value of a depth <= 2 formula (not necessarily fully modalized, if we only build depth <= 2)?\n# At top level (outside any B), we only care about fully modalized formulas of depth <= 2!\n# Wait: can a fully modalized formula of depth <= 2 be built from boolean combinations of B(psi) where psi has depth <= 1?\n# YES! By definition, a formula is fully modalized of depth <= 2 iff every atom is inside at least one B, and max nesting of B is <= 2.\n# Wait: what if there is a ~ or & between two B(psi) inside another B? That would be B(... B(psi) ...), where the inner B(psi) has depth <= 1, so the inside of the outer B STILL has depth <= 1!\n# Because if an outer B contains another B, the inner B can only have depth 1 (i.e. B(depth-0)), so the formula inside the outer B has depth <= 1!\n# Therefore, EVERY subformula of a depth <= 2 formula has depth <= 1 if it is inside ANY B, and depth <= 2 if it is outside all Bs!\n\nALL_2048 = (1 << 2048) - 1\nB_d1 = {}\n# Wait: if psi is a 2048-bit int (depth <= 1 formula), what is the semantic value of B(psi) across all possible histories?\n#Wait: for deduplicating depth <= 1 formulas (which can have depth 0 or depth 1):\n# A formula has depth 0 iff it does not contain B.\n# Let us enumerate all depth <= 1 formulas by size up to size 8!\n\nv_a, v_c, v_d = 0, 0, 0\nfor S in range(256):\n    for v in range(8):\n        idx = (S << 3) | v\n        if v & 4: v_a |= (1 << idx)\n        if v & 2: v_c |= (1 << idx)\n        if v & 1: v_d |= (1 << idx)\n\ndef b_of_d0(tt2048):\n    # Given a depth-0 formula (whose truth value only depends on v, so S=0 slice gives the 8 bits),\n    # compute the 2048-bit truth table of B(f)\n    p = tt2048 & 0xFF\n    val = 0\n    not_p = (~p) & 0xFF\n    for S in range(256):\n        if (S & not_p) == 0:\n            val |= (0xFF << (S << 3))\n    return val\n\nfor allow_consts in [False, True]:\n    # d0[s]: dict mapping 2048-bit tt -> shortest string of size s (depth 0)\n    # d1[s]: dict mapping 2048-bit tt -> shortest string of size s (depth <= 1)\n    d0 = {s: {} for s in range(1, 9)}\n    d1 = {s: {} for s in range(1, 9)}\n    seen_d0 = {}\n    seen_d1 = {}\n    \n    init = [(\"a\", v_a), (\"c\", v_c), (\"d\", v_d)]\n    if allow_consts:\n        init += [(\"T\", ALL_2048), (\"F\", 0)]\n    for name, tt in init:\n        d0[1][tt] = name\n        d1[1][tt] = name\n        seen_d0[tt] = (1, name)\n        seen_d1[tt] = (1, name)\n        \n    for s in range(2, 8):\n        # Unary ~ for d0\n        for tt, expr in d0[s-1].items():\n            ntt = (~tt) & ALL_2048\n            if ntt not in seen_d0:\n                seen_d0[ntt] = (s, f\"~({expr})\")\n                d0[s][ntt] = f\"~({expr})\"\n        # Binary for d0\n        for s1 in range(1, s - 1):\n            s2 = s - 1 - s1\n            for tt1, e1 in d0[s1].items():\n                for tt2, e2 in d0[s2].items():\n                    for op, rtt in [(\"&\", tt1 & tt2), (\"|\", tt1 | tt2), (\"->\", ((~tt1) & ALL_2048) | tt2)]:\n                        if rtt not in seen_d0:\n                            seen_d0[rtt] = (s, f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\")\n                            d0[s][rtt] = f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"\n        # Now d1: includes d0, plus B(d0[s-1]), plus ~d1[s-1], plus binary on d1\n        for tt, expr in d0[s].items():\n            if tt not in seen_d1:\n                seen_d1[tt] = (s, expr)\n                d1[s][tt] = expr\n        for tt, expr in d0[s-1].items():\n            btt = b_of_d0(tt)\n            if btt not in seen_d1:\n                seen_d1[btt] = (s, f\"B({expr})\")\n                d1[s][btt] = f\"B({expr})\"\n        for tt, expr in d1[s-1].items():\n            ntt = (~tt) & ALL_2048\n            if ntt not in seen_d1:\n                seen_d1[ntt] = (s, f\"~({expr})\")\n                d1[s][ntt] = f\"~({expr})\"\n        for s1 in range(1, s - 1):\n            s2 = s - 1 - s1\n            for tt1, e1 in d1[s1].items():\n                for tt2, e2 in d1[s2].items():\n                    for op, rtt in [(\"&\", tt1 & tt2), (\"|\", tt1 | tt2), (\"->\", ((~tt1) & ALL_2048) | tt2)]:\n                        if rtt not in seen_d1:\n                            seen_d1[rtt] = (s, f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\")\n                            d1[s][rtt] = f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"\n    print(f\"allow_consts={allow_consts}: total unique d0 up to size 7: {len(seen_d0)}, d1 up to size 7: {len(seen_d1)}\")\n'","description":"Enumerate unique depth-0 and depth-1 formulas up to size 7 using bitmasks"}}
