{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:25:13.123Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_353381","parameters":{"description":"Note fast filter using FB, CB, DB fixed histories","command":"python3 -c '\nimport time\n\n# Fast evaluator on AST directly without string parsing and with W=12!\ndef fast_check(X):\n    # X is an AST tuple\n    # First check n=0 and n=1 on FB and CB and DB!\n    # Wait: for X to be prudent, act(X, FB, n) MUST be True for ALL n >= 0!\n    # At n=0, all B(...) are True. So ev(X, 0) must be True!\n    # Against FB, if act(X, FB, m) is True for all m, then v^FB(0) = (T,T,T) and v^FB(m) = (T,T,F) for all m >= 1!\n    # And against CB, v^CB(m) = (T,T,T) for all m >= 0!\n    # And against DB, v^DB(m) = (F,F,F) for all m >= 0!\n    # WAIT A SECOND!\n    # Look at those three conditions:\n    # 1. On v^FB = ((T,T,T), (T,T,F), (T,T,F), ...), X must evaluate to True at ALL worlds n = 0, 1, 2, ...!\n    # 2. On v^CB = ((T,T,T), (T,T,T), (T,T,T), ...), X must evaluate to False for large n!\n    # 3. On v^DB = ((F,F,F), (F,F,F), (F,F,F), ...), X must evaluate to False for large n!\n    # Those three conditions DO NOT EVEN DEPEND ON X VS X!\n    pass\n'"}}
