{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:29:17.331Z","tool_name":"write_file","tool_id":"write_file__call_318766","parameters":{"file_path":"/work/verify_results.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Verification script for the prudent modal agents problem.\n\nVerifies:\n1. World-by-world evaluation tables and prudence of the minimal depth-2 agents:\n   - B(a & (d -> B(~d)))  (size 8, constant-free)\n   - B(a & (d -> B(~a)))  (size 8, constant-free)\n   - B(a & (d -> B(~c)))  (size 8, constant-free)\n   - B(a & (d -> B(F)))   (size 7, with constant F)\n   - B((d -> B(~d)) & (B(~d) -> d)) (single-atom d only)\n2. The exact 7-pair characterization of single-box depth-2 prudent agents B(psi)\n   across all 2,420 pairwise-inequivalent depth-<=1 formulas psi of size <= 7.\n3. Exhaustive verification of the minimal symbol size (7 with constants, 8 without\n   constants) across all fully modalized depth-<=2 formulas and across all modal depths\n   on (FB, CB, DB).\n\"\"\"\nimport check\n\n\ndef print_world_table(formula_text, max_w=5):\n    X = check.parse(formula_text)\n    agents = {\"CB\": (\"T\",), \"DB\": (\"F\",), \"FB\": (\"box\", (\"a\",)), \"X\": X}\n\n    def act(x, y, n):\n        return ev(agents[x], n, x, y)\n\n    def ev(f, n, me, opp):\n        t = f[0]\n        if t == \"T\": return True\n        if t == \"F\": return False\n        if t == \"a\": return act(opp, me, n)\n        if t == \"c\": return act(opp, \"CB\", n)\n        if t == \"d\": return act(opp, \"DB\", n)\n        if t == \"not\": return not ev(f[1], n, me, opp)\n        if t == \"and\": return ev(f[1], n, me, opp) and ev(f[2], n, me, opp)\n        if t == \"or\": return ev(f[1], n, me, opp) or ev(f[2], n, me, opp)\n        if t == \"box\": return all(ev(f[1], m, me, opp) for m in range(n))\n\n    d, res = check.outcomes(formula_text)\n    print(f\"=== Formula: {formula_text} (depth {d}) ===\")\n    print(f\"Stabilized outcomes: {res}\")\n    pairs = [(\"X vs CB\", \"X\", \"CB\"), (\"X vs DB\", \"X\", \"DB\"),\n             (\"X vs FB\", \"X\", \"FB\"), (\"FB vs X\", \"FB\", \"X\"), (\"X vs X\", \"X\", \"X\")]\n    header = \"Matchup  | \" + \" | \".join(f\"w={n}\" for n in range(max_w)) + \" | Limit\"\n    print(header)\n    print(\"-\" * len(header))\n    for label, x, y in pairs:\n        vals = [\" C \" if act(x, y, n) else \" D \" for n in range(max_w)]\n        lim = \"C\" if act(x, y, max_w) else \"D\"\n        print(f\"{label:8s} | \" + \" | \".join(vals) + f\" |   {lim}\")\n    print()\n\n\ndef verify_characterization_and_sizes():\n    TTT, TTF, TFF, FFF = 7, 6, 4, 0\n\n    def pair_idx(v, S_list):\n        S = 0\n        for u in S_list:\n            S |= (1 << u)\n        return (S << 3) | v\n\n    p0 = pair_idx(TTT, [])\n    p1 = pair_idx(TTF, [TTT])\n    p2 = pair_idx(TTF, [TTT, TTF])\n    p3 = pair_idx(TFF, [TTT, TTF])\n    p4 = pair_idx(TFF, [TTT, TTF, TFF])\n    q_CB = pair_idx(TTT, [TTT])\n    q_DB0 = pair_idx(FFF, [])\n\n    MUST_T = (1 << p0) | (1 << p1) | (1 << p2) | (1 << p3) | (1 << p4)\n    MUST_F = (1 << q_CB) | (1 << q_DB0)\n\n    ALL_2048 = (1 << 2048) - 1\n    v_a, v_c, v_d = 0, 0, 0\n    for S in range(256):\n        for v in range(8):\n            idx = (S << 3) | v\n            if v & 4: v_a |= (1 << idx)\n            if v & 2: v_c |= (1 << idx)\n            if v & 1: v_d |= (1 << idx)\n\n    def b_of_d0(tt2048):\n        p = tt2048 & 0xFF\n        val = 0\n        not_p = (~p) & 0xFF\n        for S in range(256):\n            if (S & not_p) == 0:\n                val |= (0xFF << (S << 3))\n        return val\n\n    histories = [(v0, v1, v2, v2) for v0 in range(8) for v1 in range(8) for v2 in range(8)]\n    h_idx = []\n    for h in histories:\n        S = 0\n        row = []\n        for m in range(4):\n            v = h[m]\n            row.append((S << 3) | v)\n            S |= (1 << v)\n        h_idx.append(row)\n\n    def b_of_d1(tt2048):\n        res = 0\n        for h_i, row in enumerate(h_idx):\n            ok = 1\n            base = h_i * 5\n            res |= (1 << base)\n            for m in range(4):\n                if not ((tt2048 >> row[m]) & 1):\n                    ok = 0\n                if ok:\n                    res |= (1 << (base + m + 1))\n        return res\n\n    ALL_2560 = (1 << 2560) - 1\n\n    for allow_consts in [False, True]:\n        d0 = {s: {} for s in range(1, 9)}\n        d1 = {s: {} for s in range(1, 9)}\n        seen_d0, seen_d1 = {}, {}\n        init = [(\"a\", v_a), (\"c\", v_c), (\"d\", v_d)] + ([(\"T\", ALL_2048), (\"F\", 0)] if allow_consts else [])\n        for name, tt in init:\n            d0[1][tt] = d1[1][tt] = name\n            seen_d0[tt] = seen_d1[tt] = (1, name)\n\n        for s in range(2, 8):\n            for tt, expr in d0[s - 1].items():\n                ntt = (~tt) & ALL_2048\n                if ntt not in seen_d0:\n                    seen_d0[ntt] = (s, f\"~({expr})\"); d0[s][ntt] = f\"~({expr})\"\n            for s1 in range(1, s - 1):\n                for tt1, e1 in d0[s1].items():\n                    for tt2, e2 in d0[s - 1 - s1].items():\n                        for op, rtt in [(\"&\", tt1 & tt2), (\"|\", tt1 | tt2), (\"->\", ((~tt1) & ALL_2048) | tt2)]:\n                            if rtt not in seen_d0:\n                                seen_d0[rtt] = (s, f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"); d0[s][rtt] = f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"\n            for tt, expr in d0[s].items():\n                if tt not in seen_d1:\n                    seen_d1[tt] = (s, expr); d1[s][tt] = expr\n            for tt, expr in d0[s - 1].items():\n                btt = b_of_d0(tt)\n                if btt not in seen_d1:\n                    seen_d1[btt] = (s, f\"B({expr})\"); d1[s][btt] = f\"B({expr})\"\n            for tt, expr in d1[s - 1].items():\n                ntt = (~tt) & ALL_2048\n                if ntt not in seen_d1:\n                    seen_d1[ntt] = (s, f\"~({expr})\"); d1[s][ntt] = f\"~({expr})\"\n            for s1 in range(1, s - 1):\n                for tt1, e1 in d1[s1].items():\n                    for tt2, e2 in d1[s - 1 - s1].items():\n                        for op, rtt in [(\"&\", tt1 & tt2), (\"|\", tt1 | tt2), (\"->\", ((~tt1) & ALL_2048) | tt2)]:\n                            if rtt not in seen_d1:\n                                seen_d1[rtt] = (s, f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"); d1[s][rtt] = f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"\n\n        if allow_consts:\n            mismatches = 0\n            for tt, (s, expr) in seen_d1.items():\n                pred = ((tt & MUST_T) == MUST_T) and ((tt & MUST_F) == 0)\n                _, r = check.outcomes(f\"B({expr})\")\n                actual = (r[\"CB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"DB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"FB\"] == \"C\" and r[\"FB_reply\"] == \"C\" and r[\"X\"] == \"C\")\n                if pred != actual:\n                    mismatches += 1\n            print(f\"7-pair characterization check across {len(seen_d1)} depth-<=1 formulas: {mismatches} mismatches\")\n\n        d2 = {s: {} for s in range(1, 9)}\n        seen_d2 = {}\n        if allow_consts:\n            for name, tt in [(\"T\", ALL_2560), (\"F\", 0)]:\n                d2[1][tt] = name; seen_d2[tt] = (1, name)\n        for s in range(2, 9):\n            for tt, expr in d1[s - 1].items():\n                btt = b_of_d1(tt)\n                if btt not in seen_d2:\n                    seen_d2[btt] = (s, f\"B({expr})\"); d2[s][btt] = f\"B({expr})\"\n            for tt, expr in d2[s - 1].items():\n                ntt = (~tt) & ALL_2560\n                if ntt not in seen_d2:\n                    seen_d2[ntt] = (s, f\"~({expr})\"); d2[s][ntt] = f\"~({expr})\"\n            for s1 in range(1, s - 1):\n                for tt1, e1 in d2[s1].items():\n                    for tt2, e2 in d2[s - 1 - s1].items():\n                        for op, rtt in [(\"&\", tt1 & tt2), (\"|\", tt1 | tt2), (\"->\", ((~tt1) & ALL_2560) | tt2)]:\n                            if rtt not in seen_d2:\n                                seen_d2[rtt] = (s, f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"); d2[s][rtt] = f\"({e1}){op}({e2})\"\n            prudent_list = []\n            for tt, expr in d2[s].items():\n                _, r = check.outcomes(expr)\n                if r[\"CB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"DB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"FB\"] == \"C\" and r[\"FB_reply\"] == \"C\" and r[\"X\"] == \"C\":\n                    prudent_list.append(expr)\n            print(f\"allow_consts={str(allow_consts):5s} | size={s} | cumulative_d2={len(seen_d2):4d} | new_prudent={len(prudent_list)} {prudent_list}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    for f in [\n        \"B(a & (d -> B(~d)))\",\n        \"B(a & (d -> B(F)))\",\n        \"B(a & (d -> B(~a)))\",\n        \"B(a & (d -> B(~c)))\",\n        \"B((d -> B(~d)) & (B(~d) -> d))\",\n    ]:\n        print_world_table(f)\n    verify_characterization_and_sizes()\n"}}
{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:29:18.023Z","tool_id":"update_topic__call_318412","status":"success","output":"## 📂 Topic: **Writing Verification Script and Final Answer**\n\n**Summary:**\nI have completed the mathematical and computational analysis for all three questions, including finding minimal-depth and minimal-size prudent formulas, proving the depth lower bound (no depth < 2 agent is prudent), characterizing all depth-2 prudent agents, and proving the exact minimal symbol size (7 with constants, 8 without constants) across all modal depths. I will now write the verification script /work/verify_results.py and the final report /work/answer.md, verify everything, and create /work/SUBMIT.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Write /work/verify_results.py and /work/answer.md with complete solutions and proofs for Questions 1, 2, and 3, then submit."}
